  "narrative": {
    "summary": "Bahrain's AI governance is led by the Information & eGovernment Authority (iGA) under the Ministerial Committee for ICT. The central instrument is the General Policy for the Use of AI (2025), which binds all government entities, adopted alongside the GCC Guiding Manual on AI Ethics. Binding obligations otherwise come from the Personal Data Protection Law (2018). There is no national AI strategy yet; the UNESCO readiness assessment (2025) recommends finalising one. A standalone AI law, proposed by the Shura Council in 2024, is still being drafted.",
    "lead_institutions": [
      "Information & eGovernment Authority (iGA)",
      "Ministerial Committee for Information and Communication Technology",
      "Personal Data Protection Authority",
      "Shura Council"
    ],
    "last_deep_review": "2026-10-06",
    "review_notes": "Deep review 2026-10-06. bahrain.bh blocks automated reading; the AI policy record now points to the iGA final version (30 July 2025). Searched with no AI-specific material found: Central Bank of Bahrain rulebook, National Cyber Security Center, standards, procurement, sandbox. The GCC Guiding Manual on AI Ethics is held in the GCC regional file and applies here automatically."
  },
